{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the implementation looks complete, but the tests leave several mandatory parts of the requirement unverified.\n\n**What the implementation covers**\n- `UsageLog::start` (`src/authoring/usage.rs`) creates `<state>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` with `create_dir_all` and `create_new`. The run id combines nanosecond time, process id and a sequence number.\n- `UsageRecord` serializes `version`, `run_id`, `project_root`, `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend`, `model`, `start_time_ms`, `end_time_ms`, `outcome`, `determination`, `evidence_output` and `evidence_written`.\n- A record starts as `outcome: \"unfinished\"` with a null end time. `finish` sets `completed`, `failed` or `cancelled`, so incomplete runs stay distinguishable from completed ones.\n- `Judgment::kind` gives only `true`, `false` or `FIXME`, so FIXME entry text never reaches the record.\n- The record stores only counts, bytes and kinds. The source-text, rationale and unknown-tool-name leak checks in the tests cover this.\n- `author_evidence_with_output` sets `evidence_output` to `file` or `stdout`. `configured_assessment` and `PendingAssessment::persisted` set `evidence_written` only after a successful write.\n- `usage_state_root` resolves symlinks and refuses a state location inside the project before creating any directory. This applies in both file and stdout mode.\n- `config::state_root` implements the `state_location` rules for XDG, `HOME` and Windows. Errors from `state_root`, `UsageLog::start` and `finish` propagate with \"cannot record usage … (evidence written: …)\" messages.\n- The code marked {impl} is marked consistently, and I found no unspecified behaviour in it beyond what `usage_inputs` and `usage_requests` specify.\n\n**What the tests cover**\n- Unit tests in `usage.rs` check the unfinished and cancelled lifecycle, the end time, `determination`, `evidence_written`, and that no source or model text is stored.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` checks:\n  - the `file` and `stdout` values of `evidence_output`;\n  - `evidence_written` for true, false and FIXME;\n  - a failed evidence write (`evidence_written` false while the accepted FIXME is kept);\n  - failed and denied-read runs;\n  - that `#125` is absent from the record;\n  - rejection of state inside the project, with no directory created.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs` checks one record per assessment in a batch, with mixed completed and failed outcomes.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. No test asserts the format version, `run_id`, `project_root`, `subject_kind` or `start_time_ms`. The `subject` field is asserted only in two batch failure tests. The requirement says the record MUST identify these, so removing or corrupting any of them would pass the suite.\n2. No test checks that the file is named `<run-id>.json` and that the name matches the record's `run_id`. Tests only read whatever file is in the directory.\n3. No test covers failure to determine or write the state location. For example, `HOME` or `XDG_STATE_HOME` may be unusable, the usage directory may be unwritable, or `finish` may fail after the evidence was written. These are the \"report the failure and don't claim history was recorded\" obligations, and the only state-failure test is the in-project refusal.\n4. The cancelled outcome is tested only by calling `finish(\"cancelled\")` in a unit test. It is not tested end to end, except possibly through the PTY interrupt test, which I did not read.\n\nBecause several mandatory fields and the state-failure behaviour have no test coverage, and no FIXME acknowledges these gaps, the determination is false.",
  "inputs": [
